Lemme try to make it more clear: Whenever an `SSLHandshakeException` happens, it reaches directly `DefaultChannelPipeline` and we get `WARN` log like this with Stacktrace:
```
18 Jun 2020 23:55:19.403 [nioEventLoopGroup-3-1] WARN  i.n.c.DefaultChannelPipeline - An exceptionCaught() event was fired, and it reached at the tail of the pipeline. It usually means the last handler in the pipeline did not handle the exception.
```

So is there any way to prevent this? Because handling the exception at ALPN Handler has no effect, it still throws Stacktrace.
